A||||2||mwbackus||Fuel Injector Rebuild
Z||000000||mwbackus||09-06-99||10:08 AM||||I've obviously got some leaky injectors and I have put off repair for some time now.  What are the options for rebuilding the injectors?  Are there rebuild(seal) kits available (part#?), and if so, can a backyard mechanic do this himself?  I know there are services for injector balancing/repair, but I would like to try replacing the seals, etc. myself since a little too much grease washed out from under my fingernails last night. :-)<p>Mike<br>88 Formula (108k)
Z||000001||theogre||09-06-99||04:49 PM||||ingectors are not reabuildable. They should be replaced in a whole set. You can replace just one but it's allot of trouble, and sometimes causes other problems.
Z||000002||mwbackus||09-06-99||06:21 PM||||Perhaps I was not clear when I stated "rebuild", what I need is the part number for the kit that includes : injector screens, end caps, and o-rings.  There are several services that will do this, but they want 25.00 a piece for the kit installation, flow testing, and ultrasonic cleaning.  Hasn't anyone done this before?  I have access to an ultrasonic cleaner, and I am sure I can rig up a makeshift bench flow tester quite easily.<p>Mike
